{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL0hvbGx5d29vZC8yMDAwLS0yMDEwL1RoZSUyME1hbiUyMFdobyUyMFNhdmVkJTIwQ2hyaXN0bWFzJTIwJTI4MjAwMiUyOS8","type":"movie","name":"The Man Who Saved Christmas","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/duVZ4pnQhJA5sZ2IXqxXvvoX5DD.jpg","description":"Alfred Carlton Gilbert invented the Erector Set and is trying to get it onto the toy shelves of the country. A.C. is startled to be summoned to the White House, where top officials ask him to convert the toy factory into a weapons manufacturing company for the duration of the war. \"No\" is really not an option, for fear of being labeled unpatriotic so the switch is made. Later, government officials ask A.C. to be their spokesman for a campaign to avoid \"toy giving\" for the coming holidays and buy war bonds instead. With a young son himself, who looks forward to Christmas like any other child, what will A.C. do this time?\n\nReleased 15 Dec 2002 · Canada, United States of America · Language: English · 100 min\n\nOn your server — Audio: English","releaseInfo":"2002","genres":["Drama","TV Movie","Hollywood"],"imdbRating":"6.2","runtime":"100 min","cast":["Jason Alexander","Kelly Rowan","Ed Asner","Jayne Eastwood","Ari Cohen","C. David Johnson","Kenneth Welsh","Daniel Kash"],"director":["Sturla Gunnarsson"],"released":"2002-12-15T00:00:00.000Z","slogan":"He couldn't stop the war, but he wouldn't let the war stop Christmas.","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Sturla Gunnarsson","character":"Director"},{"name":"Jason Alexander","character":"A.C. Gilbert","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/qRezZ2yhM2bmBERt7jVcxo8RVSA.jpg"},{"name":"Kelly Rowan","character":"Mary","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/y4j0JO71WUBoFDwrtHpjmwjtdWt.jpg"},{"name":"Ed Asner","character":"Charles Gilbert","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/AeVizz1AfAB2TbsfyzgBvqeSR3G.jpg"},{"name":"Jayne Eastwood","character":"Mrs. Gilbert","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/cL75FbJRKDdpvkOJDUg